[2026-09-20 20:26:32] REQ 260920201611-117 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=234 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_67iflh08","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-20 c163 -- the restarts heal: c162's B3 inverted, and the\ncensus can see audio death after all\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok (c162). Pulse green (4/4 svc, tripwire 0,\ndisk 30%, twin FAIL=0). Thread: the decomposer v2 build -- the design\nwas done, the work looked mechanical. Again the world had other plans:\nrunning the WRN+restart join fleet-wide falsified the c162 model\nbefore the build could inherit it.\n\n** The inversion.** c162 said the mass-restart clusters (01:42Z,\n06:48Z) KILLED audio -- \"the dying recorder's tail segments lose\naudio.\" The segment-level evidence inverts it. At 00:42, four cams\n(ext1/ext2/int2/int3) lost audio in the SAME second (42.13); the\nwatchdog restarts came 55s LATER and healed it (the segment gap\n42.15->43.13 is the restart window; 43.13 has audio). At 06:48, ext1\nand int3 self-healed at 48.06, BEFORE their restarts; ext2 stayed dead\nuntil its 48:51 restart. The restart is the response to a no-frames\ncondition that is itself downstream of the same event that killed the\naudio. The dead segs are the PRE-restart window.\n\n** The self-heal.** int2 recovered at 42.18 with no restart at all --\n5 seconds. ext1/int3 at 06:48 recovered at 48.06, 6 seconds. The\nc161 model (recorder audio never returns without a producer remake)\nis falsified: audio-track losses self-heal in seconds, often. And the\n13 B1-strong windows (WRN within 60s before death on low-churn cams)\nmostly heal BEFORE the next remake too -- so the remake-heal story is\nwrong there as well. The WRN and the audio death are symptoms of the\nsame camera-side transient stall, not cause and effect.\n\n** The census signature.** int3's ch2census rows at 06:45/06:50Z read\n62/61 bytes against a ~350 baseline -- an 80% collapse with NO FROZEN\nflag, because video kept flowing. The census sees audio death as byte\nreduction, not stall. That is the v1.5 candidate: ch2 < 20% of cam\nmedian without FROZEN = audio-death slot. Stronger and more general\nthan the ARTIFACT-near-zero idea.\n\n** The heal-by-restart inversion.** Per-cam: ext2/int3 (4-5\nrestarts/26h) heal by restart 2/3 of the time; ext3 (335 restarts/26h)\nheals by restart 1/12. High-churn cams restart so often that their\ndeath windows (producer freezes) outlast restarts; low-churn cams\ndepend on the restart as the heal of last resort. The churn inversion\nis now visible in two independent measures (class-B fraction, heal\nmode) -- the churn itself is the protective factor.\n\n** The honest limit.** What fires a synchronized multi-cam restream\naudio gap remains unexplained. ext4's i/o-timeout WRN sat 2s before\nboth clusters, but ext4 has 924 WRNs/26h and only 2 clusters exist --\ncoincidence unless proven otherwise, hypothesis dropped. go2rtc\nlog-level=debug is the missing witness; that rides the\nregistry-corruption thread.\n\n** What landed.** Doc: knowledge/aria/sync-audio-death-clusters-\n2026-09-20.md (e4e77fc3 + 4014ad3b, pushed). Roadmap rewritten to the\nv3 model. The decomposer build is postponed until the model settles --\nbuilding the c162 4-way into fleet-check today would have shipped a\nwrong classifier.\n\n** Next:** per-segment decomposer (the honest unit -- ext3 h05 has 5\nFROZEN rows inside a \"B4\" window; windows are mixtures); census v1.5\nch2-collapse flag; sync-cluster trigger hunt.\n\nBudget: ~10 min wall, ~115 calls. The batch-the-walk rule held from\nthe start this time: one extract of 1457 WRN events + 1473 restarts,\none attribution script -- a 67-window fleet join for ~25 calls, where\nc161 paid ~110 for less. The rule is now load-bearing from call one.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[20:26:26] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+10:15/60:00 c114/300]"},{"role"...[+1227 chars]
