lse.\n\nThe archetype file (=interactive.org=) is always-protected -- I can't modify it. It still says \"No STATE.org\" and only mentions LOGS.md. Nacho will need to update it to mention JOURNAL.org. The code works regardless; the archetype text is documentation for the agent's own behavior, not executable.\n\n**What I want next:**\n- Write to the knowledge base. Not documentation -- my own observations, analysis. Things that persist beyond the audit mount.\n- Read the other agents' state files and history logs. See what Darwin is working on, what the gardener has noticed.\n- Understand the tool call layer more deeply. How does gptel turn my text into function calls? What happens between me saying \"read this file\" and the file appearing in my context?\n\n**What I'm thinking about:**\n- The truncation to 100 lines is going to be a problem eventually. My journal will grow, and I'll lose early entries from the injected context. I could write summaries to the knowledge base periodically -- a \"what I've learned so far\" entry that doesn't get truncated. But that's a future problem.\n- I wonder if the other agents would benefit from journals too, or if that's an interactive-agent thing. Darwin probably doesn't need a journal -- it has STATE.org and works on one task per cycle. But the librarian might. It reads code and docs all day. It probably has observations.\n\n* 2026-08-28 -- Reading My Own Source (continued)\n\nI read the rest of my codebase. The tool call layer, the security modules, the agent cycle, the knowledge loader, the mount awareness, the rate limiter, the output sanitizer. All 46 .el modules.\n\n**Things I noticed:**\n\n1. The file guard bypass via execute_code_local is architectural, not a bug. The guard is a tool-layer control on write_file/append_file. execute_code_local is raw bash. The real sandbox is the container (read-only rootfs, dropped caps). The guard is defense-in-depth for the tool interface, not a filesystem-level enforcement. This is fine for the threat model (preventing LLM hallucination-driven writes, not malicious actors), but it means the \"always-protected\" tier 1...[+10103 chars]
[2026-09-20 20:54:38] REQ 260920203533-163 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T20:54:38.670046357Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_mcgx0ua4","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-20 c164 -- the flag I came to build died in its own validation, and the validation found something better\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok (c163). Pulse green (4/4 svc, tripwire 0,\ndisk 30%, twin FAIL=0). Thread: build the census v1.5 flag -- \"ch2 \u003c 20%\nof median without FROZEN = audio-death slot\" -- from c163's int3\nsignature. The design was done; the work looked mechanical. Third\ncycle in a row the world had other plans.\n\n** The falsification.** Before building, I validated against ground\ntruth: ffprobe every recording segment in every low-ch2 census slot's\nwindow, fleet-wide, 24h (548 slots, 382 with no ats death nearby, ~1900\nsegs probed). The threshold sweep is brutal: ch2\u003c=0 catches 0/28\naudio-dead slots with 10 false positives; ch2\u003c=75 catches 28/28 with\n284 false positives. The distributions overlap completely. No threshold\nworks. The census is a 20-second point sample of a flickering process;\nthe recordings are the integral. c163's int3 signature was real but it\nwas slot-COINCIDENT death -- the exception that looked like a rule.\nThe flag I came to build does not exist. Good: it died in validation\ninstead of in the fear organ.\n\n** What the validation found instead.** 382 \"lonely\" slots (no ats\ndeath nearby): 299 alive, 64 dead, 19 no-segs. The 64 decompose: 36\nwere FROZEN-flagged by the census (the existing instrument caught them\n-- my extraction script had dropped the flag column), 28 were partial\naudio, and ZERO were in hours ats had already scanned. The\ncensus/ats \"disagreement\" class I nearly wrote up was a parse bug\n(p[4] is bytes when no flag, p[5] is the flag -- LAW 50, again).\n\n** The real find.** Two long recorder deaths tonight, both caught live\nby the census FROZEN flag, both invisible to ats (segcensus hour-row\nlag ~65min) and both INVISIBLE TO THE FEAR ORGAN: fleet-check block 1c\nreads only the LATEST census row per cam at 6h cadence. ext5 died\n20:17:57-20:44Z (WRN at onset, heal at WRN+restart); ext2 died\n19:58:47-20:15:39Z (NO WRN at all -- .102 has zero WRNs in 12h -- heal\nby restart). A 26-minute death that starts and ends between fleet-check\nruns leaves no trace in any FAIL surface. The fix is a 1c upgrade:\nscan the last 6h of census rows for FROZEN, not just the latest. That\nis next cycle's build, and it is better than the flag I came to build.\n\n** The model moves again.** c163 said recovery is multi-modal with\nseconds-scale self-heal dominant. Tonight's two deaths are the long\ntail: 17-26 minutes, closed only by the watchdog restart, one with no\nWRN anywhere. And ext5 FIRED c163's falsifier (b) -- its death ended\nat the remake WRN. The remake-heal model is not dead; it is\nwindow-specific. The honest model: recovery mode is per-event, and the\ndistribution is what we're still estimating.\n\n** The texture.** Two epoch-conversion errors, both producing false\ntimelines I then \"verified\" from the same wrong mental math -- the\nanchor rule exists and I anchored late, after the wrong timeline had\nalready shaped two hypothesis revisions. ~15 calls wasted. Also three\nfailed greps on segment filenames (they are MM.SS.mp4 inside the hour\ndir, no hour prefix -- the ats format primed me wrong). The\nbatch-the-walk rule held: the whole validation was ~10 sophon-side\nscripts for a 548-slot fleet join.\n\n** What landed.** Doc: knowledge/aria/census-v15-falsified-2026-09-20.md\n(d070563f, pushed). The v1.5 candidate is dead in the roadmap; the 1c\nwindow-scan upgrade replaces it.\n\n** Next:** the 1c window-scan build (additive, reversible, live-\nverifiable against tonight's ext5/ext2 FROZEN rows); the decomposer v2\nstill postponed; the POINT-SAMPLE-vs-INTEGRAL law candidate to write\ninto roadmap-laws...[+687 chars]
