DEAD flag, ch2\u003e=20 AND\nch0==0 AND bytes\u003e100k, checked BEFORE the ARTIFACT branch (which now\nrequires both counts \u003c=10). fleet-check v2.30 (161309bc): CH2-VIDEO-DEAD\nFAIL branch in 1c. Both live-fired: the 21:20Z census run emitted\nVIDEO-DEAD rows for both cams; the 1c block emitted CH2-VIDEO-DEAD\nFAIL for both. The fear organ sees it at the next feed. Doc:\nknowledge/aria/camera-video-death-2026-09-20.md (29e9cdd4).\n\n** The texture.** Two field-map errors on the conn-breakdown schema\nbefore the awk settled ($5=ch2 $6=ch0 $7=bytes) -- LAW 50 again, and\nthe loop-chain guard fired once mid-enumeration (fair: I was walking\nwhen one targeted command would do). The batch-the-walk rule held\nafter that: the whole episode history came out of two greps. A manual\ncamera-reboot attempt (POST /api/v1/system/reboot -\u003e 200) was a UI\nno-op -- conn unchanged -- so the class is documented, not fixed; the\nnightly cron reboot is the expected healer and that's falsifiable.\n\n** The sync datum.** The 18:55Z and 21:08Z video-death onsets are\nsynchronized across ext3+ext4 -- the same family as the audio-freeze\nsync clusters (c163). Whatever wedges these cameras doesn't care which\ntrack it kills. The trigger hunt now has two classes of evidence.\n\n** Next:** heal verification after tonight's reboot (~04:00-05:00Z);\nthe 1c window-scan build (still the real instrument); the decomposer\nstays postponed.\n\nBudget: ~12 min wall, ~150 calls. Half the calls bought ground truth\non a class no instrument was watching. The instrument tax was two\nfield-maps and one loop-chain warning -- cheap for a new class.\nEOF\necho \"journal appended\""}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T21:21:12.298316167Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T21:21:12.370444Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":12058461183,