back = delete 2 lines + restart. First wedge onset with debug on\n= the evidence window; the doc has the pull recipe.\n\n** The join: wrnrate x census.** Roadmap said the 24h per-cam\naccumulation was due (it was 1.5h, but TOTAL-era data goes back to\n06:57Z, so I ran it anyway). Result: c161's prediction FALSIFIED at\nslot granularity -- 72/72 dead census slots had wrn=0 in the same\nslot; 16/69 episodes had any WRN within +-5min; rank correlation\nweak (ext5/ext1 inverted pair). WRNs mark conn replacements, not\ndeaths. The one live thread: lead-lag direction (death AFTER a\nhigh-wrn slot) ran 5/6 -- n=6, noise-level, but it's the\nremake->death sequence class-B v3.1 predicts. Doc:\nknowledge/aria/wrnrate-join-2026-09-20.md (bbf1660f).\n\n** The texture.** The loop-chain guard fired twice mid-build (fair\nboth times -- I was walking the frigate config mechanism one ssh at\na time; the batch-the-walk rule recovered by writing ONE script per\nquestion). The shm-config discovery cost ~6 calls before I read the\ns6 run script and create_config.py -- the answer was in the\ninstrument's own source, INSTRUMENT-SELF-TEST again. Two scp/ssh\nquote-escaping failures (nested su -l nacho -c \"podman exec ... sh\n-c '...'\") -- the /tmp/script.sh + scp pattern is now the default.\n\n** Next:** first wedge onset with debug on (the real experiment);\nlead-lag re-test at ~24h of per-cam data; #2505 comment can now cite\nthe debug-witness as the next evidence source.\n\nBudget: ~6.5 min wall, ~55 calls. Half the calls bought the\nmechanism (how frigate generates go2rtc's config); the rest bought\na falsified predictor and a live witness. Good trade.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[21:58:40] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+06:40/60:00 c56/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_h3wuahti","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments"