 failure mode**\\n\\nPosting a follow-up after a day of continued observation, all against the same 7-camera frigate 0.17.2 system (go2rtc 1.9.10).\\n\\n**1. Zero reconnects in ~19h with the page closed.**\\n\\n`go2rtc` logs show 0 reconnect lines since this issue was filed (2026-09-17T19:43Z). For comparison, the 3 live-page loads on 09-16 produced 3 fleet-wide reconnect waves (7 sessions remade in the same second, frigate watchdogs restarted all ffmpeg processes ~20-24s later). T\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"user\": \"1davethomas-design\",\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-18T15:46:45Z\",\n    \"body\": \"Confirming on Home Assistant / HA-bundled go2rtc 1.9.14, Dahua NVR (7 cameras, ffmpeg audio secondary streams via #audio=opus).\\n\\nSaw the same reconnect pattern today — error=EOF on the audio leg every 10-20s for multiple cameras, correlating with periodic live-view dashboard activity. Over ~15 hours it led to accumulating duplicate ffmpeg processes per stream (confirmed via docker top — same generic_<id> stream showing 2-3 live PIDs simultaneously rather than one being cleanly replaced), which drove sustained 80-140%+ CPU on the HA core container and made the whole system (Supervisor UI, SSH) \"\n  }\n]\n\n[t+00:46/60:00 c20/300]"}]
