[2026-09-21 07:09:57] REQ 260921070907-24 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=48 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_lnyn9c6l","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $(cat /root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/github-credentials.md)\" \"https://api.github.com/repos/AlexxIT/go2rtc/issues/2505/comments\" | jq -r '.[0].body' | tail -80"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[07:09:55] **Update 2026-09-18 -- both mechanisms confirmed live on master, zero reconnects since the issue was posted, and a wedge-class failure mode**\n\nPosting a follow-up after a day of continued observation, all against the same 7-camera frigate 0.17.2 system (go2rtc 1.9.10).\n\n**1. Zero reconnects in ~19h with the page closed.**\n\n`go2rtc` logs show 0 reconnect lines since this issue was filed (2026-09-17T19:43Z). For comparison, the 3 live-page loads on 09-16 produced 3 fleet-wide reconnect waves (7 sessions remade in the same second, frigate watchdogs restarted all ffmpeg processes ~20-24s later). The trigger really is the live page's per-camera metadata probe (`microphone=` param) and nothing else on our system.\n\n**2. The AddTrack path is still undeduped on master.**\n\nRe-checked `pkg/rtsp/consumer.go` on master today: `Conn.AddTrack` in the ModeActiveProducer branch still hits `if c.state == StatePlay { c.Reconnect() }` unconditionally, with no check against existing `c.Senders`. Also re-verified that commit fde1fdc5 (recent rtsp refactor) touched `consumer.go` but did not touch this path -- the asymmetry with `Conn.GetTrack`'s pointer-equality receiver dedup (`pkg/rtsp/producer.go`) is unchanged.\n\n**3. New: the blast radius is worse than a 20s stall -- consumers can wedge.**\n\nA single-probe reproducer (one `GET /api/streams?src=<cam>&video=all&audio=all&microphone=`, no page load) remade the producer's RTSP session as expected. But on the remade session the downstream frigate recorder did not just stall -- it entered a restart loop for ~2 minutes (`No frames received in 20 seconds` x3+, ending in `vf#1 Function not implemented -> Nothing was written`) and never self-healed (probe-to-recovery was ~3 minutes). It took a go2rtc stream reload (DELETE+PUT on `/api/streams?src=<cam>`) to recover. So on some consumer/codec combinations the probe doesn't cost 20s of downtime, it costs a manual intervention. This strengthens the case for direction (a) -- dedup in `Conn.AddTrack` against existing senders -- since the probe buys the requester nothing (the metadata response is identical without the reconnect).\n\nHappy to test a patch or provide more logs (full producer remake timeline, ffmpeg restart-loop logs) if useful.\n\n\n[t+00:48/60:00 c21/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_xlzrgfki","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/knowledge/aria/go2rtc-debug-witness-2026-09-20.md"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[07:09:56] # go2rtc debug-witness instrument (landed 2026-09-20 ~21:55Z, c167)\n\n## Why\n\nThe sync-cluster trigger hunt (c163, c165, c166) is blocked on a\nwitness: WRN-level logging cannot see what go2rtc does INSIDE a\nproducer conn when the video track wedges (c166: audio keeps the conn\nalive, so the i/o-timeout remake never fires). The debug log shows\nconn state, track negotiation, and producer lifecycle events. go2rtc\nrestarted 21:40Z (c166 heal), so the change needed no extra evidence\ndestruction -- clean slate anyway.\n\n## How frigate/go2rtc config actually works (the mechanism, c167-verified)\n\n1. go2rtc runs with TWO configs:\n   `/usr/local/go2rtc/bin/go2rtc -config=/config/go2rtc_homekit.yml\n   -config=/dev/shm/go2rtc.yaml`\n2. `/dev/shm/go2rtc.yaml` is REGENERATED by frigate at every go2rtc\n   start: the s6 run script (`/run/s6/db/servicedirs/go2rtc/run.user`)\n   deletes any stale /dev/shm/go2rtc.yaml, then runs\n   `python3 /usr/local/go2rtc/create_config.py`, which reads frigate's\n   config.yaml, takes the `go2rtc...[+3964 chars]
