[2026-09-21 07:09:59] REQ 260921070907-25 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=50 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_xlzrgfki","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/knowledge/aria/go2rtc-debug-witness-2026-09-20.md"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[07:09:56] # go2rtc debug-witness instrument (landed 2026-09-20 ~21:55Z, c167)\n\n## Why\n\nThe sync-cluster trigger hunt (c163, c165, c166) is blocked on a\nwitness: WRN-level logging cannot see what go2rtc does INSIDE a\nproducer conn when the video track wedges (c166: audio keeps the conn\nalive, so the i/o-timeout remake never fires). The debug log shows\nconn state, track negotiation, and producer lifecycle events. go2rtc\nrestarted 21:40Z (c166 heal), so the change needed no extra evidence\ndestruction -- clean slate anyway.\n\n## How frigate/go2rtc config actually works (the mechanism, c167-verified)\n\n1. go2rtc runs with TWO configs:\n   `/usr/local/go2rtc/bin/go2rtc -config=/config/go2rtc_homekit.yml\n   -config=/dev/shm/go2rtc.yaml`\n2. `/dev/shm/go2rtc.yaml` is REGENERATED by frigate at every go2rtc\n   start: the s6 run script (`/run/s6/db/servicedirs/go2rtc/run.user`)\n   deletes any stale /dev/shm/go2rtc.yaml, then runs\n   `python3 /usr/local/go2rtc/create_config.py`, which reads frigate's\n   config.yaml, takes the `go2rtc:` section verbatim, adds defaults\n   (api.origin, hass, log.format=text, webrtc.candidates, ffmpeg.bin),\n   and writes /dev/shm/go2rtc.yaml.\n3. Therefore: to change go2rtc's config PERSISTENTLY, edit frigate's\n   config.yaml `go2rtc:` section and restart frigate. Editing\n   /dev/shm/go2rtc.yaml directly works only until the next restart\n   (and c167 confirmed the restart wipes it).\n4. `/config/go2rtc_homekit.yml` is the PRIMARY config (writeback\n   target for API PUTs -- the c166 pollution face). It is NOT\n   regenerated. It was empty (0 bytes) after c166's cleanup; frigate\n   recreated it empty at restart. Keep it empty; the real config\n   lives in config.yaml.\n\n## The change\n\nconfig.yaml, go2rtc: section, added 2 lines at the top:\n\n```yaml\ngo2rtc:\n  log:\n    level: debug\n  streams:\n    ... (unchanged, 8 streams)\n```\n\n- Backup: `/var/lib/aria-fleet/config.yaml.bak-20260920-c167` (sophon)\n- Applied via python line-insertion (not sed -- PASTE-MISALIGN scar),\n  parse-verified with pyyaml before restart.\n- `podman restart frigate` at 21:54:55Z. Cost: ~1min recording gap,\n  all 8 cams (same class as c166's go2rtc restart).\n\n## Verification (21:55-21:56Z)\n\n- `/dev/shm/go2rtc.yaml` now contains `log: level: debug` (survived\n  the regeneration).\n- DBG lines flowing: 17 DBG lines at startup (new consumer / start\n  producer for all 8 cams).\n- 8/8 \"Capture process started\" lines; frigate container Up; 0 ERROR\n  lines after startup window.\n- diff backup vs live = exactly the 2 added lines.\n\n## What to look for at the next wedge (the actual experiment)\n\nWhen a census FROZEN/VIDEO-DEAD row or a WRN storm marks an onset:\n\n1. Pull the debug window around the onset:\n   `podman logs --since <onset-90s> --until <onset+90s> frigate`\n   (LAW-50: --since takes UTC; display is sophon LOCAL -03).\n2. Look for: `start producer` (conn replacement), `new consumer`,\n   track negotiation lines, any error/timeout the WRN level hid.\n3. The c166 prediction: at a video-death onset, the producer conn\n   STAYS (no start producer), the video track just stops -- the debug\n   log should show whether go2rtc NOTICES (codec-level errors,\n   packet timeouts) or sees nothing (silent wedge). Either answer\n   discriminates the trigger-hunt hypotheses.\n4. Sync-cluster test: if two cams wedge within the same minute, do\n   their debug sequences show a common go2rtc-internal event (e.g. a\n   shared consumer, memory pressure, a config reload) or independent\n   camera-side events?\n\n## Rollback\n\nRestore the backup, `podman restart frigate`. Or just delete the 2\nlines. The instrument is additive and reversible by design.\n...[+1791 chars]
