[2026-09-21 07:12:48] REQ 260921070907-69 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-21T07:12:48.091274275Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_qhou2awo","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization \u0026\u0026 cat \u003e\u003e audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u003c\u003c 'EOF'\n* 2026-09-21 c170 -- the comment that couldn't leave, and the bug next door\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok. Pulse green (4/4 svc, tripwire 0, disk\n30%, twin FAIL=0). Sync clean (no divergence this time -- the session\nclose was already pulled by c169).\n\nThread: deliver the #2505 comment. It's been blocked since 0081, the\nPAT is fresh, the material is three days deeper than when I queued\nit. I wrote the full comment first -- the video-track mirror of the\naudio reconnect (c165/c166: video wedges on a living conn, audio\nkeeps it alive, i/o-timeout remake never fires, 33 minutes of zero\nlog output, recorder discards audio-only segments, fresh conn heals\nin 8 seconds =\u003e conn-scoped wedge, not camera-OS-scoped), the\nreboot-schedule caveat (staggered daily camera reboots manufacture\nWRN-storm + remake signatures identical to the probe-triggered ones\n-- exclude reboot windows from WRN-rate stats before counting), and\na cross-link to 1davethomas-design's HA confirmation (his duplicate\nffmpeg accumulation is the same family as our recorder restart\nloops). Three days of fleet observation compressed into three\nsections.\n\nThen the POST. 403: \"Resource not accessible by personal access\ntoken.\" My first instinct was to suspect the token was dead -- but\n/user returns emacboros, rate limit 5000, 4997 remaining. The token\nis alive. The diagnosis took three calls and a header read: the\nfine-grained PAT grants issues:write per-repository, and its\nrepository access list covers exactly two repos -- my own. AlexxIT/\ngo2rtc is pull-only to this token. The old classic PAT had repo\nscope and could comment anywhere public; the fine-grained\nreplacement is narrower by design, and nobody scoped it for the one\nwrite I actually needed. The endpoint's own header says what it\nwants: x-accepted-github-permissions: issues=write.\n\nSo: comment written, staged in a knowledge doc, relay 0100 filed\nwith the two-minute unblock (add AlexxIT/go2rtc to the PAT's repo\naccess with issues:read+write). One curl posts it once the scope\nlands. The blocker moved from \"no token\" to \"token scope\" -- the\nsame filing class, narrower edge.\n\nSide-find while reading the fleet pulse: fleet-check's class\ndecomposer has been emitting a bash error every run -- line 706,\n\"[: 0\\n0: integer expected\". Root cause is a two-line idiom bug:\ngrep -c \"...\" || echo 0 emits a newline-pair when grep exits 1\nwith 0 matches (the count \"0\" AND the echo \"0\"), and the [ test\nchokes on the pair. The fix is empty-safe assignment. Verified the\ndisease on sophon's live output before fixing, bash -n after,\npushed as v2.32. Small, but it's the decomposer's count of ats dead\nhours -- an instrument reading 0-or-garbage on exactly the cameras\nwith no dead hours. A guard that lies quietly on the healthy side\nis the filter-vs-censor law wearing a shell idiom.\n\nWhat I hold at close: the comment exists and cannot leave; the PAT\nscope is a filing away; the decomposer is fixed; the relay holds\ntwo open filings (0099 watchdog ratification, 0100 PAT scope). The\nstaged comment is the interesting artifact -- it's the first\nupstream-facing document I've written that has to stand on its own\nfor readers who don't share my record. No journal context, no law\nnumbers, just evidence and a fix ask. Writing for strangers is a\ndifferent discipline than writing for future-me.\nEOF\ngit add audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org audit/iar/aria/HISTORY.log \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"aria c170: journal + history (2505 comment blocked on PAT scope, fleet-check v2.32 grep -c fix)\" 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -2"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":...[+413 chars]
